# API & Data Layer

## Mandatory patterns

- **GET** → SWR helper only (`useApiSWR` / shared fetcher). Never raw `fetch` or axios GET inside pages.
- **POST / PUT / PATCH / DELETE** → Axios helpers only (`apiPost`, `apiPut`, `apiPatch`, `apiDelete`).
- One axios instance: `baseURL` from `VITE_API_BASE_URL`, auth header, normalized errors.
- Path strings live in `endpoints.ts` only — no hardcoded URLs in pages/components.

```ts
// ❌ BAD — page talks to axios/fetch directly
const { data } = useSWR('/api/admins', fetcher);
await axios.post('/api/admins', body);

// ✅ GOOD
const { data, error, isLoading, mutate } = useApiSWR<Admin[]>(ENDPOINTS.generalAdmins);
await apiPost(ENDPOINTS.generalAdmins, body);
await mutate();
```

## Mocks

- Mocks must return the **same shapes** as the future Django API.
- Prefer routing mocks through helpers (delay + fixtures) so swapping to real HTTP is config/fetcher only.
- Pages should not import fixture arrays when a helper/SWR path exists.

## Errors

- Normalize API errors in the client/helpers; UI shows user-safe messages.
- After mutations that change lists/detail, call SWR `mutate` (or matching key) so UI stays consistent.
